{
  "$description": "Semantic foreground/background pairs that must meet WCAG 2.2 AA in every theme. 'text' needs 4.5:1; 'large-text' and 'ui' need 3:1. Tokens are dot paths into the semantic tier. Filled controls (e.g. the primary button) are not paired with the page surface: their label identifies them (WCAG 1.4.11 does not require the fill to contrast). The focus ring is dual-colour: ring-inner must contrast with the control it surrounds, ring with the inner band and the page. The outer ring (color.focus.ring) carries the 3:1 requirement on every background it can meet: the page surfaces. The inner band (color.focus.ring-inner) is guaranteed only against the primary action background. Disabled controls (color.action.disabled.*) are exempt from contrast (WCAG 1.4.3 and 1.4.11 exclude inactive components) and are deliberately quieter than enabled ones. Secondary and danger buttons are not paired with the inner band: it is a separator, and the outer ring carries the 3:1 requirement against the page.",
  "thresholds": {
    "text": 4.5,
    "large-text": 3,
    "ui": 3
  },
